- offset-allocator (https://crates.io/crates/offset-allocator)
  Sebastian Aaltonen's `OffsetAllocator`, ported to safe Rust by Patrick Walton.
  A crates.io dependency (not vendored), used in crates/arf-gpu (src/arena.rs) to
  sub-allocate one resident GPU buffer into many aligned regions. Licensed under
  MIT OR Apache-2.0.

- llama.cpp / ggml (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp)
  Licensed under MIT; Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors (see "Licence texts").
  The GGUF single-file model format and its Q4_0 / Q4_K / Q4_K_S / Q3_K / IQ3_S block
  quantization layouts. Arf reads GGUF files and losslessly transcodes these block
  formats; the format/layout understanding is derived from llama.cpp.
  PORTED SOURCE: several kernels and routines are ports of llama.cpp / ggml code,
  each marked at its definition ("port of llama.cpp ..."). Among them:
    * crates/arf-core/src/model/gguf.rs — `dequantize_row_q3_K` and
      `dequantize_row_iq3_s` (ggml-quants.c, llama.cpp 41fc7584f).
    * crates/arf-core/src/model/qwen_vision.rs — `resize_bicubic_pillow`, a port of
      llama.cpp's `img_tool::resize_pillow` (itself adapted from Pillow, below).
    * crates/arf-serve/src/http/responses.rs — the Responses API request translation and
      output shapes, after `server_chat_convert_responses_to_chatcmpl`
      (tools/server/server-chat.cpp) and `to_json_oaicompat_resp*`
      (tools/server/server-task.cpp).
    * crates/arf-gpu/src/shaders/metal/moe_mm_id_q4ks.metal (`kernel_mul_mm_id`),
      gemv_q4ks_id_msl.metal (`kernel_mul_mv_id`); matmul_vec_q4ks_msl.metal and
      matmul_mm_q4ks.metal follow ggml-metal.metal's Q4_K kernel structure;
      gated_delta_net_msl.metal and gdn_prologue_msl.metal (src/models/delta-net-base.cpp
      and the ggml ops it uses), ssm_conv1d_msl.metal (`ggml_ssm_conv`), and their WGSL
      twins under crates/arf-gpu/src/shaders/wgsl/ (e.g. matmul_vec_q4k_ggml.wgsl,
      gated_delta_net.wgsl, ssm_conv1d.wgsl).
    * the Metal residency-set and command-buffer concurrency logic in
      crates/arf-gpu/src/gpu/metal/island.rs, crates/arf-gpu/src/gpu/context.rs and
      crates/arf-gpu/src/weights.rs (ggml-metal-device.m, ggml-metal-context.m,
      ggml-metal.cpp).
    * crates/arf-serve/src/http/systemone.rs — the System One (`/v1/systemone`) request
      parsing, decision prompt inputs, temperature lookup and answer math, a port of
      tools/server/server-decision.cpp and `post_systemone` in tools/server/server-context.cpp,
      and its `tojson` follows `value_to_json` in common/jinja/value.cpp (llama.cpp a4cb4c61f, read at 050439614).

- Pillow (https://github.com/python-pillow/Pillow)
  Licensed under the MIT-CMU License (see "Licence texts").
  PORTED SOURCE (indirectly): the separable bicubic resample in
  crates/arf-core/src/model/qwen_vision.rs follows llama.cpp's port of Pillow's
  `Resample.c`, so it matches Pillow's output bit for bit.

- Splash (https://github.com/incoai/splash)
  Licensed under Apache-2.0 (the same licence text as this product's LICENSE). Splash
  ships no NOTICE file. The files below are modified versions; each says so at its top.
  The technique of running a 4-bit quantized matmul through Metal 4's
  MetalPerformancePrimitives `matmul2d` over a native `uint4b_format` tensor, with
  the affine scale/bias applied per quant group from precomputed input sums, and
  the tile-ordered weight layout that goes with it.
  PORTED SOURCE (2026-09-25): `crates/arf-gpu/src/shaders/metal/matmul_g64_msl.metal`
  is a modified port of Splash 1.0.2's group-64 decode matmul
  (`runtime/metal/kernels/common/q4_sgmatrix.h`, `decode/linear_q4_sgmatrix.metal`:
  the bf16 `128+q` simdgroup-matrix operand, the split-K last-arriving reduction and
  the gate/up epilogue), changed to take f32 activations and write f32 outputs with
  f16 scale/bias. The StorageN=256 weight layout it reads is Splash's.
  PORTED SOURCE (2026-09-25): `g64pf_mm_n128` in
  `crates/arf-gpu/src/shaders/metal/matmul_g64_pf_msl.metal` is a modified port of Splash
  1.0.2's eight-simdgroup prefill linear (`runtime/metal/kernels/prefill/linear_q4.metal`,
  `q4_mpp_prefill_tile`), changed to take f32 activations (through a bf16 operand pass) and
  write f32 outputs with f16 scale/bias.
  PORTED SOURCE (2026-09-27): `crates/arf-gpu/src/shaders/metal/matmul_g64_pfs_msl.metal` is
  a modified port of the same file's four-simdgroup prefill kernels
  (`prefill_linear_q4_n128_sg4`, `prefill_linear_q4_n128_residual_sg4`,
  `prefill_linear_q4_n128_up_silu_sums_sg4`, `q4_prefill_write_output_sums`) and its operand
  pass (`prefill_linear_q4_sums32`) — the file is identical in Splash 1.0.2 and 1.1.0 —
  changed the same way; the up-silu form keeps Splash's bf16 output and output sums.

- DFlash 2 (https://github.com/z-lab/dflash, https://huggingface.co/incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2)
  The block-diffusion speculative drafter. Arf's draft path (crates/arf-gpu/src/gpu/metal/
  dflash2*.rs, shaders/metal/dflash2_msl.metal) implements the model defined in
  `dflash/model.py` — the two-tap grouped dynamic convolution, the block-plus-context
  attention, the generate loop's context handling and the greedy candidate selector — and
  `dflash2_ref.rs` is a plain CPU reference written from that file to gate the GPU path.
  Splash's `runtime/model/DFlashDraft.cpp` was read for the Metal-side structure. The code is
  MIT (z-lab/dflash; Copyright (c) 2026 Z Lab, see "Licence texts") and Apache-2.0 (Splash);
  the draft CHECKPOINT is published by Inco AI / Z Lab under Apache-2.0 and is downloaded by
  the user, not bundled.

- FlexGEMM (https://github.com/JeffreyXiang/FlexGEMM)
  Licensed under MIT; Copyright (c) 2025 Jianfeng Xiang (see "Licence texts").
  PORTED SOURCE: the submanifold-conv neighbour map in `scripts/ref/trellis2/shim.py`
  follows FlexGEMM's torch path (`flex_gemm/ops/spconv/submanifold_conv3d.py`,
  `_compute_neighbor_cache_torch`). The shim is a reference/test harness and is not part
  of the engine. TRELLIS.2 itself (MIT) is fetched by the user, not bundled.

- Qwen chat templates and preprocessor configuration (https://huggingface.co/Qwen)
  Test fixtures under crates/arf-serve/testdata/*.jinja are the chat templates published
  with Qwen2.5 / Qwen3-Coder / Qwen3.8 checkpoints, and
  crates/arf-core/testdata/qwen_audio/preprocessor_config.json is a Qwen3-Omni
  preprocessor config, copied verbatim so rendering and feature extraction can be
  checked against the reference. They are distributed under the Apache-2.0 licence of
  the repositories they come from.

- tiny-vllm (https://github.com/jmaczan/tiny-vllm)
  Conceptual inspiration for a from-scratch, minimal vLLM-style inference engine.
  No code is taken from it. Licensed under Apache-2.0.

